Count what public SDK libraries re-export from private frameworks.

classify.py skipped PrivateFrameworks entirely and read only v4 stubs' re-export
lists. The iOS SDK's AudioToolbox.tbd is a v3 stub that re-exports the private
AudioToolboxCore, which holds AudioOutputUnitStop and most of the AudioUnit API. So
those symbols looked missing on iOS, and a build made for one executable compiled a
logging stub over the real function into the AudioToolbox adapter: Brighter Shores'
AudioOutputUnitStop would have done nothing. Private frameworks are now read and
folded into the public libraries that re-export them (v3 and v4), then dropped, so
they never become a library of their own. Generic builds were not affected.
Upstream candidate: brand-free; it only turns false "missing" results into "present".

